open Quiver

/-!
# A group acting cocompactly on a tree is finitely presented

The target of this file is

`Work.ORBassSerre.Action.isFinitelyPresented_of_isCocompact_tree`:
a group acting cocompactly on a non-empty tree, with finitely presented vertex stabilisers and
finitely generated edge stabilisers, is finitely presented.

The proof runs through the Bass--Serre structure theorem: `G` is the fundamental group of the
finite graph of groups obtained by taking the quotient `V/G`, and a finite graph of finitely
presented groups (over finitely generated edge groups) has a finite presentation.

This file records the graph-of-groups data attached to a `G`-tree: the vertex groups
(stabilisers of chosen vertex-orbit representatives), the edge groups (stabilisers of the
chosen lifts of the edge orbits), and the two maps of an edge group into the vertex groups
(`edgeGroupToSrc`, given by inclusion, and `edgeGroupToTgt`, given by conjugation by the edge
element of `fg_of_isCocompact_tree`).
-/

/-!
## Proof plan (Bass--Serre structure theorem)

The proof of the main theorem follows the classical route, in the following pieces.

* **Graph of groups data.**  For each vertex orbit `A` the vertex group `vertexGroup A`
  (the stabiliser of a chosen representative) and for each edge orbit `E` the edge group
  `edgeGroup E` (the stabiliser of a chosen lift `edgeLift E`), with the two maps
  `edgeGroupToSrc E` (inclusion) and `edgeGroupToTgt E` (conjugation by `edgeElt E`) into the
  source and target vertex groups.  These are recorded above/below.

* **A fundamental domain.**  One chooses a spanning tree `T` of the quotient graph `V/G`
  together with a lift to a subtree `Y ⊆ V` (one lift per vertex orbit, one lift per
  edge orbit of `T`), and for each edge orbit not represented by an arrow of `Y` a lift with
  source at a lifted vertex, whose "stable letter" is the corresponding element of `G`.

* **The presentation.**  `G` is generated by the vertex groups of the fundamental domain
  together with the stable letters, subject to the amalgam relations along the tree edges and
  the HNN relations along the remaining edges; this group is the fundamental group of the
  quotient graph of groups, and it has a finite presentation because the vertex groups are
  finitely presented and the edge groups are finitely generated.

* **The key input** is the *normal form / reduced word* theorem for the graph of groups: a
  reduced word maps to a non-trivial element of `G`.  Its proof follows the path argument on
  the given tree `V` (a reduced word gives a reduced path in `V` from the base vertex to the
  translate of the base vertex, and a reduced closed path in a tree is trivial).

* **Inversions** are handled by passing to the barycentric subdivision of `V` (whose vertex
  stabilisers are the vertex stabilisers of `V` and the *setwise* edge stabilisers), where the
  action is without inversions; the setwise edge stabilisers are finitely generated (index at
  most two over the oriented edge stabilisers) and are amalgamated along the (finitely
  generated) oriented edge stabilisers, which is what makes the subdivided graph of groups
  finitely presentable.

## Status

Already available in the workspace (proved separately, `Submission.Work.ORBassSerre.Action.*`):

* `Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.isFinitelyPresented_of_amalgam_case`: the case of two
  vertex orbits joined by one geometric edge orbit (the amalgam case).  Its proof reduces to the
  HNN case or proves the amalgam normal form via `Monoid.PushoutI.NormalWord` and a *walk*
  argument on `V`, using `Work.ORBassSerre.Tree.Seg.arrow_unique` (a tree has at most one arrow
  between two given vertices).
* `Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.isFinitelyPresented_of_hnn_case`: the case of one vertex
  orbit and one geometric edge orbit (the HNN case).  Proof: Mathlib's
  `HNNExtension.ReducedWord` normal form (Britton's lemma) plus the walk argument.
* `Work.ORBassSerre.Action.isFinitelyPresented_of_finiteIndex_subgroup`: finite presentability
  passes up from a finite-index subgroup.
* `Work.ORBassSerre.Action.fg_of_isCocompact_tree`: `G` is finitely generated (with the
  explicit generating set `⋃_A S_A ∪ {edgeElt E}`), and this file exports the canonical-lift
  machinery (`orbitRepV`, `orbitRepE`, `srcE`, `tgtE`, `edgeLift`, `edgeLt_left`,
  `edgeLift_right`, `edgeElt`).
* `Work.ORBassSerre.FP.pushoutI_isFinitelyPresented` and `...FP.hnn_isFinitelyPresented`.

## What remains

1. A "fundamental domain" datum: a lift of every vertex orbit, a set of *tree* arrows spanning
   the quotient graph and lifting to a subtree of `V`, and for each remaining edge orbit a lift
   with source at a lifted vertex together with its stable letter.  (A convenient encoding of
   the spanning tree is a parent map `par : orbitV G V → orbitV G V` together with a rank
   function decreasing along `par`, plus distinctness of the edge orbits of the chosen lifts.)
2. Surjectivity of the resulting presentation `π₁ → G` (the generating set of
   `fg_of_isCocompact_tree` is contained in the images of the vertex groups and the stable
   letters).
3. The normal form theorem: a reduced word in the presentation that is not a single vertex-group
   letter has a non-trivial image in `G`.  Proof: associate to the word a walk in `V` whose
   vertices are the images of the partial products applied to the lifted representatives; the
   walk has no immediate backtrack (each step uses a *different* arrow at each vertex, by
   `arrow_unique`), and the last vertex of the walk is `φ(w) • (lifted vertex)`; if `φ(w) = 1`
   the walk is closed and reduced, hence trivial by `IsTree`.
4. Finite presentability of the presentation: immediate from the explicit finite presentation,
   since the vertex groups are finitely presented and the edge groups are finitely generated.
5. Inversions: for the barycentric subdivision the action is inversion-free, but the new
   ("midpoint") vertex stabilisers are the *setwise* edge stabilisers, which are only finitely
   generated (index at most two over the oriented edge stabilisers, see
   `Work.ORBassSerre.Action.isFinitelyPresented_of_unorderedStabilizer` for the exact
   hypothesis: it needs the oriented stabiliser itself to be finitely presented).  So the
   inversion-free case must be proved in a form that allows vertex groups which are merely
   finitely generated when they arise as "midpoints" amalgamated along a finitely generated edge
   group; in the amalgam `M *_{C_e} U_e` with `U_e = <C_e, τ>` (τ inverting the edge) the
   relations of `U_e` over `C_e` are finitely many, and the internal relations of `C_e` are
   already present because `C_e ⊆ M`.
-/

universe u v

variable {G : Type*} {V : Type*} [Group G] [Quiver V] [Quiver.HasInvolutiveReverse V]
  [MulAction G V] [Work.ORBassSerre.GraphAction G V]

/-- The vertex group of a vertex orbit: the stabiliser of its chosen representative. -/
noncomputable abbrev vertexGroup (A : Work.ORBassSerre.orbitV G V) : Subgroup G :=
  MulAction.stabilizer G (orbitRepV (G := G) (V := V) A)

/-- The edge group of an edge orbit: the stabiliser of the chosen lift of the orbit. -/
noncomputable abbrev edgeGroup (E : EdgeOrbit G V) : Subgroup G :=
  MulAction.stabilizer G (edgeLift (G := G) (V := V) E)

/-- The edge group of `E` fixes the source of the canonical lift, hence is contained in the
vertex group of the source orbit. -/
theorem edgeGroup_le_vertexGroup_src (E : EdgeOrbit G V) :
    edgeGroup (G := G) (V := V) E ≤ vertexGroup (G := G) (V := V) (srcE (G := G) (V := V) E) := by
  intro g hg
  rw [MulAction.mem_stabilizer_iff] at hg ⊢
  rw [← edgeLift_left (G := G) (V := V) E, ← GraphAction.smul_left g (edgeLift (G := G) (V := V) E)]
  exact congrArg Quiver.Total.left hg

/-- The edge group of `E`, conjugated by the edge element, is contained in the vertex group of
the target orbit. -/
theorem edgeGroup_le_conj_vertexGroup (E : EdgeOrbit G V) :
    edgeGroup (G := G) (V := V) E ≤
      (vertexGroup (G := G) (V := V) (tgtE (G := G) (V := V) E)).map
        (MulEquiv.toMonoidHom (MulAut.conj (edgeElt (G := G) (V := V) E))) := by
  intro g hg
  rw [MulAction.mem_stabilizer_iff] at hg
  have hfix : g • (edgeLift (G := G) (V := V) E).right = (edgeLift (G := G) (V := V) E).right := by
    rw [← GraphAction.smul_right g (edgeLift (G := G) (V := V) E)]
    exact congrArg Quiver.Total.right hg
  rw [← MulAction.stabilizer_smul_eq_stabilizer_map_conj (edgeElt (G := G) (V := V) E)
    (orbitRepV (G := G) (V := V) (tgtE (G := G) (V := V) E))]
  rw [MulAction.mem_stabilizer_iff, ← edgeLift_right (G := G) (V := V) E]
  exact hfix

/-- The inclusion of the edge group of `E` into the vertex group of the source. -/
noncomputable def edgeGroupToSrc (E : EdgeOrbit G V) :
    edgeGroup (G := G) (V := V) E →* vertexGroup (G := G) (V := V) (srcE (G := G) (V := V) E) :=
  Subgroup.inclusion (edgeGroup_le_vertexGroup_src (G := G) (V := V) E)

/-- If `V` is a tree, then so is the quotient graph `V/G` *connected* (the quotient of a
connected graph is connected); it is of course not a tree in general. -/
theorem orbitV_nonempty_path (hT : Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree V)
    (A B : Work.ORBassSerre.orbitV G V) :
    Nonempty (Quiver.Path A B) := by
  obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Quotient.exists_rep A
  obtain ⟨b, hb⟩ := Quotient.exists_rep B
  subst hb
  obtain ⟨p⟩ := hT.1 a b
  exact ⟨(Work.ORBassSerre.orbitPrefunctor (G := G) (V := V)).mapPath p⟩

/-- A group acting cocompactly on a non-empty tree, with finitely presented vertex stabilisers and
finitely generated edge stabilisers, is finitely presented.  (This is the "finite graph of
finitely presented groups is finitely presented" result in the language of tree actions.)

## Proof

Everything is reduced to the inversion-free case by *lifting the whole situation to a common
universe*.  The presentation-chain lemmas in `Structure/` index edge orbits by
`Work.ORBassSerre.orbitE G V`, whose declared universe forces the arrows of `V` and the group `G`
to live in the *same* universe; the statement of the present theorem does not impose that
relation.  The file `Action/Lift/Basic.lean` therefore constructs, for `G : Type u`,
`V : Type v` and arrows of `V` in `Type w`,

* the lifted vertex type `Lift.VLx G V = ULift.{max u v w} V`,
* its lifted quiver (arrows `ULift.{max u v w} (a ⟶ b)`, reversal lifted from that of `V`), and
* the lifted group `Lift.LGroup G V = ULift.{max u v w} G`,

all of which live in the same universe `max u v w`, together with the lifted action and graph
action (`instMulAction`, `instGraphAction`).  The transfers `Lift.isTree_VLx`,
`Lift.isCocompact_VLx`, `Lift.isFinitelyPresented_stabilizer_VLx` and `Lift.fg_stabilizer_VLx`
carry the hypotheses over to the lifted setting, where the whole presentation chain applies
verbatim; finally `Lift.isFinitelyPresented_of_LGroup` descends finite presentability to `G`.

Concretely, the proof splits on `Nonempty (Quiver.Total V)`: if there are no arrows, `V` is a
single point, `G` is that vertex stabiliser and `Structure.isFinitelyPresented_of_isEmpty_total`
applies; otherwise one takes the colour subgroup `H` of the lifted tree (of finite index, with
the same stabilisers, acting without inversions), applies the inversion-free theorem
`Structure.isFinitelyPresented_of_noInversions` to `↥H`, and concludes with
`isFinitelyPresented_of_finiteIndex_subgroup` and `Lift.isFinitelyPresented_of_LGroup`.
-/
theorem isFinitelyPresented_of_isCocompact_tree {G : Type*} {V : Type*} [Group G] [Quiver V]
    [Quiver.HasInvolutiveReverse V] [MulAction G V] [Work.ORBassSerre.GraphAction G V]
    [Nonempty V] (hT : Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree V) (hcc : Work.ORBassSerre.IsCocompact G V)
    (hstab : ∀ v : V, Group.IsFinitelyPresented (MulAction.stabilizer G v))
    (hedge : ∀ e : Quiver.Total V, Group.FG (MulAction.stabilizer G e)) :
    Group.IsFinitelyPresented G := by
  classical
  by_cases harrow : Nonempty (Quiver.Total V)
  · -- Pass to the lifted setup, where the arrows live in the same universe as the group.
    haveI : Nonempty (Lift.VLx G V) := ⟨Lift.VLx.up (Classical.choice ‹Nonempty V›)⟩
    have hT' : Work.ORBassSerre.IsTree (Lift.VLx G V) := Lift.isTree_VLx (G := G) hT
    have hcc' : Work.ORBassSerre.IsCocompact (Lift.LGroup G V) (Lift.VLx G V) :=
      Lift.isCocompact_VLx (G := G) hcc
    have hstab' : ∀ a : Lift.VLx G V,
        Group.IsFinitelyPresented (MulAction.stabilizer (Lift.LGroup G V) a) :=
      Lift.isFinitelyPresented_stabilizer_VLx (G := G) hstab
    have hedge' : ∀ e' : Quiver.Total (Lift.VLx G V),
        Group.FG (MulAction.stabilizer (Lift.LGroup G V) e') :=
      Lift.fg_stabilizer_VLx (G := G) hedge
    -- The colour subgroup of the lifted tree has finite index and acts without inversions,
    -- with the same stabilisers.
    obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ :=
      Work.ORBassSerre.Tree.Walk.bipartition_exists (V := Lift.VLx G V) hT'
    let H : Subgroup (Lift.LGroup G V) :=
      Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.colourSubgroup (G := Lift.LGroup G V) c
    haveI : H.FiniteIndex :=
      Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.finiteIndex_colourSubgroup (G := Lift.LGroup G V) hT' hc
    have hstabH : ∀ a : Lift.VLx G V, Group.IsFinitelyPresented (MulAction.stabilizer ↥H a) :=
      fun a => Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.isFinitelyPresented_stabilizer_subgroupOf
        (Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.stabilizer_le_colourSubgroup hT' hc a) (hstab' a)
    have hedgeH : ∀ e : Quiver.Total (Lift.VLx G V), Group.FG (MulAction.stabilizer ↥H e) :=
      fun e => Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.fg_stabilizer_subgroupOf
        (le_trans (Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.stabilizer_edge_le_left e)
          (Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.stabilizer_le_colourSubgroup hT' hc e.left))
        (hedge' e)
    have hccH : Work.ORBassSerre.IsCocompact ↥H (Lift.VLx G V) :=
      Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.isCocompact_of_finiteIndex H hcc'
    haveI : Work.ORBassSerre.IsCocompact ↥H (Lift.VLx G V) := hccH
    haveI : Finite (Work.ORBassSerre.orbitV ↥H (Lift.VLx G V)) := hccH.1
    haveI : Fintype (Work.ORBassSerre.orbitV ↥H (Lift.VLx G V)) := Fintype.ofFinite _
    haveI : Finite (Work.ORBassSerre.orbitE ↥H (Lift.VLx G V)) := hccH.2
    haveI : Fintype (Work.ORBassSerre.orbitE ↥H (Lift.VLx G V)) := Fintype.ofFinite _
    -- The Bass--Serre presentation of the inversion-free action of `H` is finitely presented
    -- and maps isomorphically onto `H`.
    have hfp : Group.IsFinitelyPresented ↥H :=
      Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.isFinitelyPresented_of_noInversions (G := ↥H)
        (V := Lift.VLx G V) hT' hccH
        (Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.actsWithoutInversions_colourSubgroup
          (G := Lift.LGroup G V) hc) hstabH hedgeH
    -- Hence the lifted group, and therefore `G` itself, is finitely presented.
    have hLG : Group.IsFinitelyPresented (Lift.LGroup G V) :=
      Work.ORBassSerre.Action.isFinitelyPresented_of_finiteIndex_subgroup H
    exact Lift.isFinitelyPresented_of_LGroup (G := G) (V := V) hLG
  · exact Work.ORBassSerre.Action.Structure.isFinitelyPresented_of_isEmpty_total (G := G) (V := V)
      hT ⟨fun X => harrow ⟨X⟩⟩ hstab


end Work.ORBassSerre.Action
